[2026-03-14T22:09:16.895Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y3JjGK5UqEGYXQsM69gSkw","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a command-line tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's the complete reference:\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\n1. Visit https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Set `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings (interactive if no IDs provided) |\n| `list` | Display local recordings with status |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings (`-a` for all) |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Show CLI and browser version info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps with grouping options |\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\nRecord a session:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\nUpload a recording:\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nRun Replay MCP Server for debugging in Claude by configuring the HTTP server endpoint with your `REPLAY_API_KEY` authorization header.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed information."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad503268-e133-4807-8fc2-652411f1db75","uuid":"75f23105-19bf-4474-9543-62cbaa75d977","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a command-line tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's the complete reference:\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\n1. Visit https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Set `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings (interactive if no IDs provided) |\n| `list` | Display local recordings with status |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings (`-a` for all) |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Show CLI and browser version info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps with grouping options |\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\nRecord a session:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\nUpload a recording:\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\n\nRun Replay MCP Server for debugging in Claude by configuring the HTTP server endpoint with your `REPLAY_API_KEY` authorization header.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed information.","durationMs":3418,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T22:09:16.989Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013GV5gmZ9QT3GYaq3ZBuWsY","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. According to the documentation, it allows you to \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Investigation Approach\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured methodology:\n1. Frame your investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and validate hypotheses with gathered data\n5. Support conclusions with evidence\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code investigation.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred through dependency tracking and state inspection.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as a database of execution points—\"a specific point in the execution of the app\" where JS statements execute or significant events occur. DOM elements are also tracked independently across their lifetimes.\n\n## Practical Recommendation\n\nThe documentation emphasizes that \"the Logpoint tool is extremely useful\" for tracking expression values across execution points to identify unexpected behavior patterns."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad503268-e133-4807-8fc2-652411f1db75","uuid":"f5912c2d-08f9-4552-b9ee-8fdbf64c50d7","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. According to the documentation, it allows you to \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Investigation Approach\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured methodology:\n1. Frame your investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and validate hypotheses with gathered data\n5. Support conclusions with evidence\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code investigation.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred through dependency tracking and state inspection.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as a database of execution points—\"a specific point in the execution of the app\" where JS statements execute or significant events occur. DOM elements are also tracked independently across their lifetimes.\n\n## Practical Recommendation\n\nThe documentation emphasizes that \"the Logpoint tool is extremely useful\" for tracking expression values across execution points to identify unexpected behavior patterns.","durationMs":3038,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
