[2026-03-14T22:19:49.469Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AHPKTUjrwwSMEKFGgVJmq2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 5 tests pass consistently. Here's a summary of what I fixed:\n\n**Root cause 1: URL path parsing in Netlify functions**\nAll Netlify functions used `segments[3]` to extract resource IDs from the URL path, assuming the rewritten URL format (`/.netlify/functions/properties/:id`). However, `netlify dev` passes the original URL (`/api/properties/:id`), so `segments[3]` was `undefined`. This caused the property detail endpoint to fall through to the list endpoint, so the property detail page never loaded (no `amenities-list` element found).\n\n**Fix:** Changed all functions (`properties.ts`, `bookings.ts`, `property-images.ts`, `favorites.ts`, `users.ts`, `reviews.ts`) to find the function name in the path segments and take the next segment as the ID, which works with both URL formats.\n\n**Root cause 2: Amenity display ordering**\nThe first test expected \"WiFi\", \"Kitchen\", and \"Pool\" to all be visible in the initial 10 amenities, but alphabetical sorting put Pool as the 11th item. Also, only Essentials and Features categories had items in the first 10, missing Safety and Location headings.\n\n**Fix:** Added priority-based sorting within categories (common amenities like WiFi, Kitchen, Pool shown first) and proportional distribution of initial display slots across categories.\n\n**Root cause 3: Database needed re-seeding** \nThe seed data defined 18 amenities for property b2222222 but only 8 were in the database. Re-seeded to match.\n\n<DONE>"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332,"cache_read_input_tokens":72332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":332,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad503268-e133-4807-8fc2-652411f1db75","uuid":"8c55d296-4608-473b-a8e9-65c727278845"}
[2026-03-14T22:19:49.496Z] {"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":654351,"duration_api_ms":364128,"num_turns":78,"result":"All 5 tests pass consistently. Here's a summary of what I fixed:\n\n**Root cause 1: URL path parsing in Netlify functions**\nAll Netlify functions used `segments[3]` to extract resource IDs from the URL path, assuming the rewritten URL format (`/.netlify/functions/properties/:id`). However, `netlify dev` passes the original URL (`/api/properties/:id`), so `segments[3]` was `undefined`. This caused the property detail endpoint to fall through to the list endpoint, so the property detail page never loaded (no `amenities-list` element found).\n\n**Fix:** Changed all functions (`properties.ts`, `bookings.ts`, `property-images.ts`, `favorites.ts`, `users.ts`, `reviews.ts`) to find the function name in the path segments and take the next segment as the ID, which works with both URL formats.\n\n**Root cause 2: Amenity display ordering**\nThe first test expected \"WiFi\", \"Kitchen\", and \"Pool\" to all be visible in the initial 10 amenities, but alphabetical sorting put Pool as the 11th item. Also, only Essentials and Features categories had items in the first 10, missing Safety and Location headings.\n\n**Fix:** Added priority-based sorting within categories (common amenities like WiFi, Kitchen, Pool shown first) and proportional distribution of initial display slots across categories.\n\n**Root cause 3: Database needed re-seeding** \nThe seed data defined 18 amenities for property b2222222 but only 8 were in the database. Re-seeded to match.\n\n<DONE>","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ad503268-e133-4807-8fc2-652411f1db75","total_cost_usd":2.2934785000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":64542,"cache_read_input_tokens":2968226,"output_tokens":16002,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"